{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0001820721","cik":"0001820721","slug":"array-technologies-820721","name":"Array Technologies, Inc.","ticker":"ARRY","exchanges":["Nasdaq"],"sector":"Semiconductors & Related Devices","sic":"3674","country":"NM","website":"","listed_years":5.4,"first_annual":"2021-03-10","last_filing":"2026-07-30","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001820721&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["Array Technologies, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Semiconductors & Related Devices\", based in NM, and has been publicly reporting for 5 years.","It reported $1.3bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, down 26.1% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 28.2%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($50.8m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Gross margin expanded from 25.3% to 28.2% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820721/000162828026031453/0001628280-26-031453-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031453"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $50.8m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820721/000162828026031453/0001628280-26-031453-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031453"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.1% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820721/000162828026031453/0001628280-26-031453-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031453"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue fell 26.1% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820721/000162828026031453/0001628280-26-031453-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031453"},{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 55.8% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820721/000162828026031453/0001628280-26-031453-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031453"},{"text":"Shareholders' equity is negative (-$214.4m) - liabilities exceed assets on the balance sheet.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820721/000162828026031453/0001628280-26-031453-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031453"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.4% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820721/000162828026037190/0001628280-26-037190-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 20.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.2,"consecutive":2,"current":0.282,"current_display":"28.2%","threshold_display":"20.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -41.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","com